<!--
  Dog lens art — original, authored in this repo, Apache 2.0 (swarm decisions.md, lens 3).

  Floppy ears plus a snout, drawn as a PROP: the middle is deliberately empty so the subject's own
  face shows through between the ears. `features = null` on Lens.Dog.

  The 290x213 viewport is a 0.7345 aspect and MUST stay in sync with Lens.Dog's artAspect.

  Everything is positioned in the face frame first and then converted, so the numbers are checkable
  rather than eyeballed. With widthInUnits = 2.90 the viewport is exactly 100 units per face unit,
  and with upInUnits = 0.385 the art's top edge sits 1.45 units above the eye line:

      face unit -> viewport y  =  (1.45 - u) * 100          centre line: x = 145

      crown      +1.25  ->  y =  20
      eye line    0.00  ->  y = 145
      nose        -0.42 ->  y = 187
      art bottom  -0.68 ->  y = 213

  THE CONSTRAINT THAT SET THE EAR POSITIONS. An eye sits about 0.40 units off the centre line
  (Lens.kt's KDoc records that interpupillary is ~0.8 of eye-to-mouth), i.e. x = 105 and x = 185.
  The head edge is at 0.775 units, x = 42.5 and x = 247.5. So each ear has to live in the band
  between them — outboard enough to clear the eye, inboard enough to still touch the head. These
  ears run x = 12..86 and x = 204..278, clearing the eyes by 0.19 units on each side.

  A first draft put the inner edges at 0.34 units and the schematic preview
  (swarm/tools/preview_lens.py) showed them sitting straight on top of both eyes. That is the whole
  reason the previewer exists — it is arithmetic, so it did not need a face to catch it.

  Deliberately NOT here: the animated drop-tongue of the canonical Snapchat dog lens. That needs a
  second sticker plus mouth-open detection plus animation state, which is a scope increase both
  agents refused. Static ears and snout still read as "the dog filter".
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="145dp"
    android:height="107dp"
    android:viewportWidth="290"
    android:viewportHeight="213">

  <!-- Ear outers. Attached at the crown, bellying outward past the head edge, rounding to a soft
       tip just below the eye line. Left and right are exact mirrors about x = 145. -->
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FF8C5A32"
      android:pathData="M76,22
                        C48,26 16,58 12,102
                        C9,132 22,156 44,153
                        C68,150 84,128 85,100
                        C86,68 88,32 76,22 Z
                        M214,22
                        C242,26 274,58 278,102
                        C281,132 268,156 246,153
                        C222,150 206,128 205,100
                        C204,68 202,32 214,22 Z" />

  <!-- Ear inners, inset so a rim of the outer colour always reads as the edge of the ear. -->
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FF5E3A1E"
      android:pathData="M76,42
                        C56,48 34,74 31,106
                        C29,128 38,144 52,141
                        C66,138 76,120 77,98
                        C78,74 82,50 76,42 Z
                        M214,42
                        C234,48 256,74 259,106
                        C261,128 252,144 238,141
                        C224,138 214,120 213,98
                        C212,74 208,50 214,42 Z" />

  <!-- Snout. Centred on the face's centre line and sitting on the subject's own nose: it spans
       -0.22 to -0.62 units, below the eyes and well clear of the mouth at -1.0. -->
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FF221C18"
      android:pathData="M145,167
                        C161,167 173,175 173,186
                        C173,198 160,207 145,207
                        C130,207 117,198 117,186
                        C117,175 129,167 145,167 Z" />

  <!-- Nostril dimples and one specular highlight — the cheapest cue that reads as "wet nose"
       rather than "black blob" at carousel size. -->
  <path
      android:fillAlpha="0.55"
      android:fillColor="#FF000000"
      android:pathData="M135,180 A4,6 0 1 1 135,181 Z
                        M155,180 A4,6 0 1 1 155,181 Z" />
  <path
      android:fillAlpha="0.30"
      android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
      android:pathData="M131,174
                        C138,171 152,171 159,174
                        C152,177 138,177 131,174 Z" />
</vector>
